   "id": "niddah.63a.11",
   "daf": "63a",
   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "וְצָרִיךְ לְכַסְכֵּס שָׁלֹשׁ פְּעָמִים. בָּעֵי רַבִּי יִרְמְיָה: אַמְטוֹיֵי וְאֵתוֹיֵי חַד, אוֹ דִלְמָא אַמְטוֹיֵי וְאֵתוֹיֵי תַּרְתֵּי? מַאי? תֵּיקוּ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «And one must rub» each and every one of the substances «three times. Rabbi Yirmeya raises a dilemma» with regard to this rubbing: Is the «going and coming» of the hand over the surface of the rubbed item considered «one» rubbing, «or perhaps» the «going and coming» are considered «two» actions and two distinct rubbings? «What» is the correct count? The Gemara states: The dilemma «shall stand» unresolved."
  }
 ],
